# git's built-in union driver keeps both sides' appended lines instead of
# raising a conflict, so a grow-only list merges clean when two branches each
# add a line at the same end. It is safe only for a list that only grows:
# where one side rewrites or deletes and the other edits, union keeps both
# texts silently.
#
# internal/testpolicy/gitfree.txt says "This list only grows", and every
# RejectConflict on it costs a polecat rebase, so it gets the rule.
#
# Never add merge=union for anything else in this tree: unconverted.txt,
# realgit.txt, docker.txt and overbudget.txt shrink; the guardlint, cmdtree
# and beadsfake (raw bd) baselines are rewritten; CHANGELOG.md and
# docs/testing.md are prose whose edits union would duplicate.
# TestUnionMergeOnlyOnGrowOnlyLists (internal/testpolicy) fails any
# merge=union path whose file does not carry the grow-only header.
internal/testpolicy/gitfree.txt merge=union
